    <h2>2. Data collected</h2>
    <h3>Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      When this site is accessed, the hosting provider automatically collects information that
      the browser transmits (IP address, browser type and version, referring URL, time of
      request). These data are stored for security purposes (e.g., to detect and respond to
      attacks) and are deleted after 7 days.
    </p>
    <h3>Cookies</h3>
    <p>
      This site uses a single essential cookie to remember whether the visitor has acknowledged
      the cookie notice. No analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies are used.
    </p>
    <h3>Contact form</h3>
    <p>
      When the contact form is used, the submitted data (name, email, message) are processed
      solely to respond to the enquiry. Data are deleted no later than 12 months after the last
      exchange unless legal retention obligations apply.
    </p>

    <h3>AI chat widget</h3>
    <p>
      This site offers an optional chat widget (bottom-right of every page). It answers factual
      questions about Bernd&rsquo;s services, focus areas, and engagement history, grounded in the
      publicly visible content of this site.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>What is sent: only the messages you type, plus the immediately preceding turns of the
        same conversation (capped at the last 10 turns).</li>
      <li>What is <strong>not</strong> sent: your IP address, cookie identifiers, browsing
        history, contact-form submissions, or any other personal data.</li>
      <li>Where it is processed: messages are forwarded to Anthropic (anthropic.com), the
        provider of the Claude language model used to generate replies. See Anthropic&rsquo;s
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li>Retention on this site: zero. The conversation lives only in your browser&rsquo;s memory
        while the page is open and is discarded as soon as you reload or close the tab. Nothing
        is written to a database here.</li>
      <li>Retention at Anthropic: see Anthropic&rsquo;s policy linked above. The site does not
        opt into training-data use.</li>
      <li>You are free to ignore the widget entirely. No data is sent unless you actively type
        and submit a message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in providing visitor information)
      and, where applicable, Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR (consent through use of the feature).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Processing of server log data is based on Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in
      secure operation). Processing of contact form data is based on Art. 6 (1)(b) GDPR
      (pre-contractual measures) or Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR (consent).
    </p>

    <h2>4. Recipients</h2>
    <p>The following processors act on the controller&rsquo;s behalf:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> — hosting and serverless function execution.
        See their <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Anthropic PBC</strong> — AI chat replies (only if the chat widget is used).
        See their <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No data are passed to third parties outside these processing relationships.</p>

    <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel Inc. (United States) and Anthropic PBC (United States) process data outside the
      European Economic Area. Both providers are certified under the EU-US Data Privacy
      Framework. In addition, Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) per Art. 46 (2) GDPR apply
      to the data processing relationships with both providers.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
      <li>Right to withdraw consent at any time (Art. 7 (3) GDPR)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority — typically the data
      protection authority of the federal state in which you reside. For Berlin this is the
      Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Updates</h2>
    <p>
      This privacy policy may be updated to reflect changes in this site or in legal
      requirements. The current version is always available at this URL.
    </p>
